  "title": "MIMED2024: Motor Imagery MIMED dataset from Wirawan et al. 2024",
  "description": "The MIMED dataset contains EEG recordings of motor imagery and motor execution for six activities (raising and lowering each hand, standing and sitting) from 30 healthy participants. Data were acquired with a 14-channel Emotiv EPOC X headset at 128 Hz over two sessions per subject. This BIDS re-release via MOABB exposes a folder-level 3-class imagery task (left hand, right hand, trunk).",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a 14-channel Emotiv EPOC X headset (saline felt sensors, standard 10-20 montage) at 128 Hz. Each participant completed 2 sessions of 6 runs, with video-cued trials of 4 s. The source recordings were originally distributed as EDF files and as MAT files; the MAT files were reformatted to BIDS with HED event annotations.",
